IMPORT prelude

-- Section 4 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): standard definitions, one table entry for each defined term.
-- Generated from the text file; each entry carries the term as printed, the other forms of it the section prints,
-- how the Act introduces the definition, the words before its limbs, the limbs themselves (lettered paragraphs, or the
-- whole text after the keyword), and how the limbs are joined.
--
-- A thing is tested against an entry by `a thing falls within the Act's definition`.
-- "means" is a closed definition: a thing that does not meet it is not the term (JUST FALSE).
-- "includes" is open: a thing that meets a limb is the term (JUST TRUE), and any other thing is NOTHING.
-- "has the same meaning as in" another Act points outside the sources: whether the thing meets the other Act's meaning is an input.
-- The five entries that are "means ... and includes" are not read by the general rule (NOTHING); where the Act's words allow more,
-- they are read by the dedicated functions at the foot of this module, or by sa-interpretation-time.l4 ("day", "month", "year", "business day", "public holiday").

§ `Section 4 -- Standard definitions`

DECLARE `How the Act introduces a definition` IS ONE OF
    `introduced by "means"`
    `introduced by "includes"`
    `introduced by "means" and then "includes"`
    `introduced by "has the same meaning as"`

DECLARE `How the limbs of a definition are joined` IS ONE OF
    `the limbs are alternatives`
    `the limbs are listed items, each of which applies`
    `there is a single limb`

DECLARE `Defined term` HAS
    term                                         IS A STRING
    `all the forms of the term as printed`       IS A LIST OF STRING
    `how introduced`                             IS A `How the Act introduces a definition`
    `the words before the limbs are a condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    limbs                                        IS A LIST OF STRING
    `how the limbs are joined`                   IS A `How the limbs of a definition are joined`
    `line in the text file`                      IS A NUMBER

-- src:103 | Act means—
-- src:104 | (a) an Act of the Parliament of South Australia or an Act or ordinance of some earlier legislative authority in South Australia; or
-- src:105 | (b) an Act of the Imperial Parliament that has been received into the law of South Australia or applies to South Australia by paramount force;
@ref s 4 "Act" (src:103-105)
`s 4 definition 1` MEANS `Defined term` WITH
    term IS "Act"
    `all the forms of the term as printed` IS (LIST "Act")
    `how introduced` IS `introduced by "means"`
    `the words before the limbs are a condition` IS FALSE
    limbs IS (LIST "an Act of the Parliament of South Australia or an Act or ordinance of some earlier legislative authority in South Australia", "an Act of the Imperial Parliament that has been received into the law of South Australia or applies to South Australia by paramount force")
    `how the limbs are joined` IS `the limbs are alternatives`
    `line in the text file` IS 103

