-- Look a term up by any of the forms the section prints for it.
GIVEN `the term` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Defined term`
`the Act's definition of` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (`prints this term`) `the defined terms of section 4`
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `the first` FOLLOWED BY `the rest` THEN JUST `the first`
    WHERE
        `prints this term` entry MEANS elem `the term` (entry's `all the forms of the term as printed`)

-- Whether a thing falls within a definition, given the facts: whether the words before the limbs are met (ignored if the
-- entry's words before the limbs are not a condition), and, for each limb in order, whether the thing meets it.
-- For an entry that "has the same meaning as in" another Act, the first fact is whether the thing meets the other Act's meaning.
-- src:102 | In every Act and legislative instrument—
@ref s 4 (src:102)
GIVEN entry IS A `Defined term`
      `the words before the limbs are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `which limbs are met, in order` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a thing falls within the Act's definition` MEANS
    CONSIDER entry's `how introduced`
        WHEN `introduced by "means"` THEN JUST (`the conditions are met`)
        WHEN `introduced by "includes"` THEN IF `the conditions are met` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `introduced by "means" and then "includes"` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `introduced by "has the same meaning as"` THEN JUST `the words before the limbs are met`
    WHERE
        `the conditions are met` MEANS
                (IF entry's `the words before the limbs are a condition` THEN `the words before the limbs are met` ELSE TRUE)
            AND `the limbs are met`
        `the limbs are met` MEANS
            CONSIDER entry's `how the limbs are joined`
                WHEN `the limbs are alternatives` THEN or `which limbs are met, in order`
                WHEN `the limbs are listed items, each of which applies` THEN or `which limbs are met, in order`
                WHEN `there is a single limb` THEN or `which limbs are met, in order`

GIVEN `the term` IS A STRING
      `the words before the limbs are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `which limbs are met, in order` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a thing falls within the Act's definition of a term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Act's definition of` `the term`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST entry THEN `a thing falls within the Act's definition` entry `the words before the limbs are met` `which limbs are met, in order`

GIVEN `the term` IS A STRING, `the form` IS A `How the Act introduces a definition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Act's definition of a term is introduced in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Act's definition of` `the term`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST entry THEN entry's `how introduced` EQUALS `the form`

GIVEN `the term` IS A STRING, `the number of limbs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Act's definition of a term has this many limbs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Act's definition of` `the term`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST entry THEN count (entry's limbs) EQUALS `the number of limbs`

-- The five terms the Act defines with "means ... and includes", and their own readings.

DECLARE `A place` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth of Australia`
    `Norfolk Island`
    `the Territory of Christmas Island`
    `the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands`
    `another external Territory`

-- src:117 | Australia means the Commonwealth of Australia and, when used in a geographical sense, includes Norfolk Island, the Territory of Christmas Island and the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands, but does not include any other external Territory;
-- src:138 | Commonwealth means the Commonwealth of Australia and, when used in a geographical sense, includes Norfolk Island, the Territory of Christmas Island and the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands, but does not include any other external Territory;
@ref s 4 "Australia" and "Commonwealth" (src:117-138)
GIVEN place IS A `A place`, `used in a geographical sense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a place is within Australia or the Commonwealth` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
        WHEN `the Commonwealth of Australia` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `another external Territory` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `Norfolk Island` THEN IF `used in a geographical sense` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `the Territory of Christmas Island` THEN IF `used in a geographical sense` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands` THEN IF `used in a geographical sense` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:226 | sitting day, in relation to a House of Parliament, means a day on which the House actually sits (provided that, in a case where the sittings of a House on a particular day continue after midnight on that day and into the following day before the House stands adjourned, that portion of the following day prior to the adjournment of the House will be counted as a continuation of the preceding sitting day and not as a new sitting day);
@ref s 4 "sitting day" (src:226)
GIVEN `the House actually sits on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only sitting on the day is the part after midnight of a sitting that began the day before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a day is a sitting day of a House` MEANS
    `the House actually sits on the day` AND (NOT `the only sitting on the day is the part after midnight of a sitting that began the day before`)

